+# CI Run #4532 Triage — R42 Landing Failed the Index Preflight on main and Was Force-Pushed Out of main's Ancestry, 2026-10-28
+
+**Failed run:** [40630708168](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/actions/runs/40630708168) (run number #4532, head `d9d9385`, branch `main`, 04:09:17Z) · **Deliverable:** WO [#1953](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1953) — `docs(ci): R42 link-integrity gate` (serves issue #1938) · **Class:** `scripts/ops/_INDEX.md` drift, occurrence #3 (see §5), first-ever **post-landing eviction** · **No mirror issue exists** (verified 04:16Z / 04:33Z / 04:40Z board sweeps) — this document is the incident record.
+
+**Verdict:** No defect in the R42 deliverable's design is demonstrable from surviving evidence, and main is healthy at tip. What IS demonstrable: the landing commit `d9d9385` failed `⚡ Step 1: Fast Lint & Syntax Preflight` with the generated-index guard message `_INDEX.md differs from the regenerated index (512 live scripts found)`, and within ~74 seconds of that failure main was force-pushed back to `d75596d` (the pre-R42 base), evicting `d9d9385` **and** the later `7f8d8df` (gitleaksignore direct-push, two green runs) from main's ancestry. Both evicted commits are now unfetchable from GitHub even by explicit SHA. Consequences that need action: (1) the R42 deliverable is **absent from main** while its work order still reads `bridge:queued` with an **empty verdict history** — the author agent has no failure signal on their feedback channel; (2) the only durable record of `d9d9385`'s content is the CI run metadata — this report preserves what remains observable.
+
